    "Range: v7 308 top (كتاب الصيد, PDF 309; header malformed «٤ كتاب الصيد») to v7 317 end («…فلا يدل على جهله», last matn line of PDF 318). Next lesson (2025-10-11) should start at v7 318 frac 0.0: «قال: وإن أدرك المرسل الصيدَ حياً: وجب عليه أن يذكيه، وإن ترك تذكيته حتى مات: لم يؤكل، وكذا البازي والسهم» — the teacher says at 0:30:41–0:30:51 that the dhabh details (when slaughter is required) come next class, then the arrows (الرمي) chapter. Fractions use the matn-line count per page (308: 7 lines, 309: 7, 310: 6, 311: 7, 312: 10, 313: 9, 314: 7, 315: 7, 316: 10, 317: 11). Teacher's page: 1840 in his copy (0:00:30); colleagues' 1756.",
    "Transcript: only lines starting with [h:mm:ss] at column 0 used (498). The opening stretch has seven consecutive lines all stamped [0:00:30] (the model draft in the file places them at ~0:00:03–0:00:27); card 1 tags them only as U('0:00:30') with no finer precision. There is no real line before 0:00:30. Similarly 0:08:36 (×5) and 0:08:37 (×4) share stamps for the Arabic reading of «وتعليم الكلب… وتعليم البازي…». The teacher's Arabic readings around 0:21:34–0:29:54 appear only as lines prefixed «ع: [h:mm:ss]» (not line starts) and are not tagged; the Urdu translation lines that follow them are. A real-looking fragment «[0:10:00] یہ امام ابو حنیفہ، امام محمد، امام ابو یوسف کی رائے ہے اور امام صاحب سے بھی ایک رائے ہے» is glued to the end of a draft line, not a line start; not tagged (book: «عندهما، وهو رواية عن أبي حنيفة»).",
    "Card 2: OCR v7 310 reads «استثنى من ذلك الأسد والذّئب» and 311 «والذُّبِّ لخساسته»; the standard Hidaya text is «الأسد والدب» (bear), which matches the teacher's «ریچھ» (0:04:43) and the damma-shadda in «الذُّبِّ»; card writes «[الدب]» (QA confirmed: both OCR forms misread «الدُّبّ»; the wolf is listed separately in العناية ٩/٤٤). OCR «الحِدَّة» = «الحِدَأة» (kite, چیل). Teacher 0:05:09–0:05:10 says «پرندوں میں چیل جو ہے، گدھ، گدھ کا استثناء کیا ہے» and 0:05:23 «کچھ نے گدھ کا استثناء کیا ہے» — vulture (گدھ) for الحدأة is a slip; he does say چیل first, so the lughat cites U(0:05:09); the گدھ slip is not used, and 0:05:23 is tagged only for «باقی سارے جانوروں… جائز، لیکن ضروری ہے». His attribution («بعضهم» = «کچھ نے») is correct. Teacher glosses ذي ناب as «ڈاڑھوں والے» (0:06:30); card gives «کچلی» with his word in brackets.",
    "Card 3: teacher 0:10:36–0:10:38 calls the three-times view «ظاہر الروایہ» — not in matn/footnotes; the matn ascribes the زنِ غالب view to Abu Hanifa «على ما ذكر في الأصل» (a ظاهر الرواية book) and the three-times view to the Sahibayn and one riwaya of Abu Hanifa (البناية: رواية القدوري). 0:10:38 is not tagged. Teacher's Musa/door-knocking/khiyar examples (0:09:23–0:09:41) match الكفاية ٩/٤٧ (Mabsut). «ابن عباس» athar: teacher 0:08:05 (for the three times); matn says the whole ta'lim rule «مأثور عن ابن عباس»; نصب الراية calls it غريب.",
    "Card 4: the 'if found alive slaughter, if dead eat' wording of the Adi hadith (0:14:05–0:14:16) is the teacher's; the book only says «لما روينا من حديث عدي». The teacher's reason for requiring a wound (maybe it picked up a dead animal or strangled it, 0:15:08–0:15:29) is his own; card labels it «استاد» and gives the book's reasons. Teacher (0:17:21) attributes permissibility of what the dog ate from to Malik and Shafi'i without «قوله القديم», and frames it as 'once trained, later eating doesn't matter' — matn: «حجة على مالك، وعلى الشافعي في قوله القديم في إباحة ما أكل الكلب منه»; card gives the book's scope.",
    "Card 5: teacher slips not tagged: 0:18:38 «تین دفعہ ہو یا دو دفعہ ہو» (the other riwaya is the hunter's زنِ غالب, not two times; matn «على اختلاف الروايات كما بيناها في الابتداء»); 0:20:53 «تین دفعہ کھا لینا» (Abu Hanifa's argument is about eating once now). The wilderness case is «بالاتفاق» in the matn; the teacher's 'احتیاطاً حرام' (0:20:42) is the matn's reasoning given within the sahibayn's argument («فحرمناه احتياطاً»), consistent.",
    "Card 6: teacher's case (0:22:44 «اس کے بعد اس نے جا کے شکار کر لیا اپنی مرضی سے») is the one البناية ١١/٤٨٦ calls obviously haram for lack of irsal; the book's case is that it came back and then hunted. 0:22:44 is not tagged; card gives the matn and the footnote. The book has «صقراً»; teacher calls it باز.",
    "Card 7: teacher reads «ولو ألقى بعد ما نهس» (0:30:00); matn «ولو ألقى ما نَهَسَه». Footnote البناية ١١/٤٨٩ ends «فكان ذلك من غاية حماقته» (likely «حذاقته»); not used. No exam hints in this lesson.",
